# ANRI-Aerospace: repository content is stored and checked out as LF only.
#
# Rationale: recorded SHA-256 values must be reproducible on every platform.
# If a Windows checkout rewrites text files to CRLF, every recorded digest of a
# text artifact becomes wrong on Linux (and vice versa).  See the
# RO-CDFV-001-Ref-01B review report, finding F1.
#
# The explicit `-text` form is deliberate: `text eol=lf` still lets
# `core.autocrlf=true` smudge the working tree to CRLF, whereas `-text`
# disables all end-of-line conversion so the working tree always matches the
# committed bytes on Windows and on Ubuntu alike.

* -text

*.py    -text
*.md    -text
*.json  -text
*.csv   -text
*.yml   -text
*.yaml  -text
*.txt   -text
